          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"karm. if its sense can be conveyed by a Bah. So this way of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"defending the form is not very satisfactory. See, however, our\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"note on \u0924\u0941\u0932\u094d\u092f\u0917\u0928\u094d\u0927\u093f\u0937\u0941 Rag. IV. 45. \u091c\u0941\u0917\u0941\u092a\u094d\u0938\u093f\u0924\u2014censured, condemned.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0928\u093f\u0930\u0941\u092a\u092e\u0966-Avya; \u0966\u0930\u0938\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0940\u0924\u094d\u092f\u093e v. l. see com.; ( eating it ) with a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"relish the flavour of which is unparalleled. \u0928 \u0936\u0919\u094d\u0915\u0924\u0947\u2014has no fear\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"or misgiving; does not think that he is doing something censur-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"able or disgusting. \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0917\u094d\u0930\u0939\u092b\u0932\u094d\u0917\u0941\u0924\u093e\u2014the worthlessness of one\u2019s\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"belonging. The fig. here is \u0905\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0930\u0928\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0938\u2014Def. \u0938\u093e\u092e\u093e\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0902 \u0935\u093e \u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937\u094b\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093e \u0924\u0926\u0928\u094d\u092f\u0947\u0928 \u0938\u092e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0964 \u092f\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u0938\u094b\u093d\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0930\u0928\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0938\u0903 \u0938\u093e\u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e\u094d\u092f\u0947\u0923\u0947\u0924\u0930\u0947\u0923 \u0935\u093e \u0964 Where a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"particular proposition is corroborated by a general proposi-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"tion or a general proposition is supported by a particular\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"instance either under a resemblance or a contrast, that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"is Artha'ntarany\u00e2sa or corroboration. There is also \u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0902\u0938\u093e\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"in the first three lines.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words and transliteration diacritics are difficult to distinguish.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 10. \u0936\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0902-\u0936\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0938\u094d\u092f\u0947\u0926\u0902 of S'iva. Bhag\u00eeratha, a king of the solar\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"race, wishing to procure the salvation of his 60,000 ancestors that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"had been reduced to ashes by Kapila\u2019s curse, propitiated, by his\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"penance, Gang\u00e2, and induced her to come down to the earth.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"The river complied with his request but directed him to find\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"out some one who would bear her force as she would fall down\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"from heaven. Bhag\u00eeratha then propitiated S'iva who agreed to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"allow the river to fall on his head. Bh\u00e2g\u00eerath\u00ee, accordingly,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"fell from heaven on S'iva\u2019s head, thence descended to the peak\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"of Himalaya, thence to the earth and thence to the nether world\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"where her waters sanctified the offspring of Sagara. The whole\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"story is given in R\u00e2ma. I. 35-44. For \u092a\u0936\u0941\u092a\u0924\u093f\u0966\u2014some read \u092a\u0924\u0924\u093f\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"\u0936\u093f\u0930\u0938\u0903 \u0924\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f\u0924\u093f\u0927\u0930\u092e\u094d ( his i. e. S'iva\u2019s mountain). \u092e\u0939\u0940\u0927\u094d\u0930\u2014\u092e\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0927\u0930\u0924\u0940\u0924\u093f,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"\u0927\u0943 + \u0915 ( \u0905 ); a mountain. \u0905\u0927\u094b\u0927\u0903\u2014The Ganges comes down to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":16,\"text\":\"a lower and lower position. \u0938\u094d\u0924\u094b\u0915\u2014low, base. \u0905\u0925\u0935\u093e\u2014or rather,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":17,\"text\":\"what wonder if. \u0935\u093f\u0935\u0947\u0915\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f\u093e\u0928\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014Gang\u00e2, in her arrogance thought\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":18,\"text\":\"that she would bear down even S'iva and enter into the nether\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":19,\"text\":\"world with him; she was punished for this by S'iva. See R\u00e2m.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":20,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093f\u0928\u093f\u092a\u093e\u0924\u0903\u2014Mark the double entendre on this word which means\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":21,\"text\":\"( i ) great fall, and ( ii ) destruction, ruin. \u0936\u0924\u092e\u0941\u0916\u2014applies to\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit readings, especially the variant on lines 13\u201314, are unclear.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 7 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"10\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r3\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
